{% import "macros.njk" as macros with context %}

<h1>Compilation</h1>

{{ macros.endpointPath(endpoints.endpoints.buildsSync.methods, endpoints.endpoints.buildsSync.path) }}
<p class="page-lead">{{ endpoints.endpoints.buildsSync.summary }}</p>

<p>
  The request carries a <em>compilation specification</em>: the LaTeX compiler
  to use, the resources (the LaTeX sources and their dependencies — images,
  bibliographies, included files…) and build options. Three input modes are
  supported, all served by the same endpoint:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><a href="#get-querystring">GET querystring</a> — small documents, quick one-liners;</li>
  <li><a href="#post-json">POST JSON</a> — the richest mode, suited to server code;</li>
  <li><a href="#post-multipart">POST multipart/form-data</a> — upload local or binary files directly.</li>
</ul>

{{ macros.callout("note", "<p>Only one input mode is supported per request. With the GET mode, resource
values travel in the URL: prefer the JSON or multipart modes for documents larger
than a few kilobytes.</p>") }}

<p>
  On success the response body is the generated PDF (HTTP <code>201</code>).
  On failure the response is a JSON payload with the error and the compiler
  logs (<a href="#response">see the response reference</a>).
</p>

