<h3 id="resources">Resource entries</h3>

<p>
  The <code>resources</code> list describes the files uploaded and compiled
  server-side. The file arborescence is reconstructed from the
  <code>path</code> properties, so relative references
  (<code>\include{chapters/intro}</code>, <code>\includegraphics{logo.png}</code>…)
  work as in a local compilation. Each entry takes:
</p>

{{ macros.paramTable(endpoints.resourceFields) }}

{{ macros.callout("warning", "<p>Each entry must have <strong>exactly one</strong> source field:
<code>content</code>, <code>file</code>, <code>url</code> or <code>cache</code>
— else <code>MULTIPLE_RESOURCE_SOURCES</code> is returned. The <code>git</code>
and <code>tar</code> source fields are accepted by the schema but
<strong>not yet implemented</strong> server-side.</p>") }}

{{ macros.codeTabs(endpoints.endpoints.buildsSync.modes[1].samples, "samples-json") }}

